But #title-screen uses .screen display flex; centered by default. Override.

Add a "play" highlight: `.big-btn#btn-play{...}` add ▶ and pulsing glow. Make the button larger with a play triangle.

Mobile: media max-width 700: center content with background dark overlay full. `.title-inner{text-align:left;max-width:100%;padding-right:18px}`. Actually on mobile, the town would be mostly hidden behind content; add stronger gradient and maybe position content bottom. Use:
