content.text:
But this source intensity 5 always on, even during day and when room hidden. It might be selected when near and affect; fine.

Now light pool count 5. In jumpscare cutscene, cine lights (2) + killer axe + flashlight + 5 pool = 9 point lights, but cutscene may have world emergency sources too. Still much better than 20.

Need make sure setLighting 'day' sets powerLights on and emergency 0. Emergency sources inactive so pool ignores. Day outdoor has street glows 9 etc, so pool selects nearest including street, outdoor lamp, facade wash, police etc. Good.

`updateLightPool` picks nearest including through walls; e.g., inside school, outdoor lights at x58-130 might be nearest if near exit; could waste slots. But 5 nearest includes corridor lights. Fine. Should maybe skip sources outside current area, but not needed.

Now adaptive DPR. Add to Game constructor and animate. Implement:
- in init after renderer setSize: `this.baseDpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio||1, 1.5); this.renderDpr=this.baseDpr; this.frameAccum=0; this.frameCount=0; this.qualityTimer=0;`
Actually `setPixelRatio` set before. Let's add fields in constructor.
- In animate, after dt compute `this.trackPerf(dt)`.
- method:
```
trackPerf(dt) {
 if (dt<=0) return;
 this._perfAcc=(this._perfAcc||0)+dt; this._perfN=(this._perfN||0)+1;
 if (this._perfAcc < 1.6) return;
 const fps=this._perfN/this._perfAcc; this._perfAcc=0; this._perfN=0;
 const base=this.baseDpr||1;
 if (fps<42 && this.renderDpr>0.85) { this.renderDpr=Math.max(0.85,this.renderDpr-0.15); this.applyDpr(); }
 else if (fps>57 && this.renderDpr<base) { this.renderDpr=Math.min(base,this.renderDpr+0.1); this.applyDpr(); }
}
applyDpr(){ this.renderer.setPixelRatio(this.renderDpr); this.renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight); }
```
Caution: dt is clamped to 0.05, so a 10fps frame gives dt 0.05 and seems 20fps not 10. Use real elapsed from clock? clock.getDelta returns actual but clamped. We compute raw = this.clock.getDelta(); dt = min(0.05,raw). Use raw for perf. Modify animate:
```
const raw = this.clock.getDelta();
const dt=Math.min(0.05,raw);
this.trackPerf(raw);
```
- `applyDpr` on title too? title renderer same and resize. The adaptive applies globally. Fine.
- Don't oscillate: only adjust every 1.6s; decrease if fps<45, increase if fps>58 and renderDpr<base. Min 0.85.

Title `this.title.render(this.renderer)` may reset size? title has its own scene and camera but uses same renderer. resize called at init and on resize. `applyDpr` calls setSize which resets viewport; title render uses its own? It probably calls renderer.setSize in title.resize. Check.

