content.text:
Actors array is EMPTY in shot index 2! Why? `enterShot` doesn't build actors; `play` builds shots by calling `buildShots()` which invokes introShots(cine) — actors are created at that time. `this.actors` should be populated. But we forcibly set index 2 after play; however `play` might have already finished the intro? Wait after clicking play, the intro is running. At time we set index 2, maybe cinematic already completed? No.

Wait `introShots(cine)` returns shot array and creates actors before returning. But `this.actors = []` is reset in `play()` BEFORE calling buildShots? Let's check play order: lines 132 `this.shots = buildShots();` at 132, then 137 `this.actors = [];` at after! Indeed:
```
this.shots = buildShots();
...
this.actors = [];
this.lights = [];
this.extra = [];
while group.children... remove
```
So actors created inside buildShots are immediately cleared! That's a bug. Similarly lights created during introShots (world.setLighting etc.) get cleared? `cine.light` adds to group and this.lights; actors too. Then play resets actors/lights and clears group. So all intro actors vanish. This likely has been the case all along: intro cutscenes show no characters! That matches user: "make classmates characters with all animation in pop quiz" — they weren't there at all. Great catch.

Fix order: clear actors/lights/group BEFORE buildShots, but shots creation may need group cleared. Move block before `this.shots = buildShots()`. Also `buildShots` may reference `this.total` etc. Fine.

In play():
```
this.actors=[];
this.lights=[];
this.extra=[];
while group children remove;
this.shots=buildShots();
```
But `introShots` uses `world.setLighting`, and `cine.light` added to group after clearing. Good. Also `UI` etc.

Patch.

}

// ── lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────
async play(name, buildShots, opts = {}) {
  if (this.active) return false;
  this.active = true;
  this._ended = false;
  this.name = name;
  this.shots = buildShots();
  this.index = 0;
  this.shotT = 0;
  this.total = 0;
  this.flags = 0;
  this.actors = [];
  this.lights = [];
  this.extra = [];
  while (this.group.children.length) this.group.remove(this.group.children[0]);
  this.group.visible = true;

  this.game.state = 'cutscene';
  this.game.setInputActive(false);

