Add label distance management at the end of animate (and for downed too). We can compute distance to camera. The nameSprite is a child of the model; set visible/size. Let's add a helper in animate:

```
const spr = this.model.userData.nameSprite;
if (spr) {
  const cam = this.game.camera.position;
  const d = Math.hypot(this.pos.x-cam.x, this.pos.z-cam.z);
  const show = !this.controlled && !this.dead && !this.downed && d > 1.6 && d < 16;
  spr.visible = show;
  if (show) {
    const s = Math.max(0.32, Math.min(0.72, d*0.05));
    spr.scale.set(s, s*0.25, 1);
    spr.position.y = 1.96;
  }
}
```
But `nameSprite.visible` is set elsewhere; fine.

Also don't show labels through walls? Could check `world.losBlocked`, but that would hide useful labels. Keep simple.

Then player spawn: adjust.

Also the bots spawn at (-10.6,0.2), (-6.8,-0.6), (-11.4,-1.5). Player at (-8,-0.55) facing +x. Bot at -6.8,-0.6 is 1.2m in front -> giant label and body. Change to:
- player (-8.0, 0.9) facing -π/2 (+x east). Actually the objective key is "outside Room 101" — Room 101 door is at x -9..-7 on z=3 (south corridor wall) near the player. Player facing east sees the corridor. Key likely spawned near the door in the corridor.
- bots at (-11.5, 2.0), (-12.6, -1.2), (-14.0, 0.8) behind the player (west).
